(
"MK1 AGREEMENT WITH TODAY`S LAMBDA (loaded beside arest; the kernel`s forms are arest`s). <store> to the fact types of the kernel`s P whose rows are not, as a set, what today`s system:pop_rows reads over today`s booted store; ka:n the count of each kind.",
DEF("ka:fts", S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FILE")), A("k:boot"))))),
DEF("ka:differ", S5(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), A("ka:same"), K(PHI()), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)))), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("ka:fts"), S3(A("CONS"), A("k:boot"), A("id"))))),
DEF("ka:same", S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:pop"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))))),
DEF("ka:n", S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("ka:fts")), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("ka:differ")))),
"<store> to <fact type, rows the kernel holds that today does not, rows today holds that the kernel does not> for each differing fact type, and ka:extra the fact types where the kernel holds rows today does not.",
DEF("ka:dir", S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:pop"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:pop"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2))))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("ka:differ"), S3(A("CONS"), A("k:boot"), A("id")))))),
DEF("ka:extra", S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(N(0)))), K(PHI()), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")))), A("ka:dir"))),
"THE MK1 AGREEMENT LAW. The kernel never holds a row today`s lambda does not (ka:extra is empty), and the fact types whose rows differ are the 31 whose rows today`s boot adds and MK1 does not build yet: the schema reflected as the metamodel`s facts (Fact Type has Role and Object Type plays Role in part, the readings, the constraint spans and types, the Functions` Domains, the instance reflection), and the populations derived by rules (the machine`s statuses and transitions, Constraint is semantic and machine decidable, Predicate is bound, Federation is compiled, Operation awaits a driver). A new difference fails it. It failed first with an empty chunk read as a row: 281 of the 338 fact types then differed, many holding a row today did not.",
DEF("ka:expected", K(S(A("FactTypeHasRole"), A("ObjectTypePlaysRole"), A("ObjectTypeHasWorldAssumption"), A("ReadingIsPrimary"), A("RoleIsUsedInReading"), A("FactTypeHasReading"), A("ConstraintSpan"), A("ConstraintSpanHasSequenceNumber"), A("ConstraintSpanHasPosition"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionHasLocalName"), A("FunctionIsDeclaredInDomain"), A("ConstraintHasModalityOfModalityType"), A("ConstraintHasText"), A("ConstraintIsSemantic"), A("ConstraintIsMachineDecidable"), A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType"), A("FederationIsCompiled"), A("PredicateIsBound"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsProperlyOfObjectType"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsMostSpecificallyOfObjectType"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceHasReference"), A("OperationAwaitsADriver"), A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), A("TransitionExitsStatusInStateMachineDefinition"), A("StatusIsRootedInStateMachineDefinition"), A("StatusIsEffectiveInitialInStateMachineDefinition"), A("StatusIsLeafInitialInStateMachineDefinition"), A("StatusHasEffectiveTransitionToStatusOnEventType"), A("StatusReachesStatusInStateMachineDefinition")))),
DEF("ka:law", S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("ka:extra")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), A("ka:differ")), A("ka:expected"))))))
)
